@startuml

title A first schedule: registration, firing and notification

actor "the operator" as operator
participant "the scheduler" as scheduler
database "the firing record" as record
participant "whatever watches\nthe subject" as watcher

operator -> scheduler : register a job\n(the name, the expression,\nthe action kind, the subject)

note over scheduler
    The name is the natural key, so registering
    the same name again updates the one job
    instead of adding a second.
end note

... the next occurrence arrives ...

scheduler -> scheduler : the job is due
scheduler -> record : record the firing as starting\n(the job, the point, the moment)
scheduler -> watcher : publish on the subject\n(no reply is read)
watcher --> watcher : receive the notification
scheduler -> record : record the outcome\n(succeeded, or failed with the reason)
operator -> record : read the executions\nand the live status

note over scheduler, watcher
    Nothing has to answer the subject.
    The message is the notification.
end note

@enduml
